+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </div>
+</div>
+<div id="faq-intro" class="container py-4 py-md-5">
+  <div class="row">
+    <div class="col-12 col-md-10">
+      <p class="mb-0">This page answers some of the most frequently asked questions about the Postgres Community Association. If you have any additional questions, please do not hesitate to email the PGCA at <a href="mailto:board@postgres.ca" class="font-weight-normal">board@postgres.ca</a>.
+      </p>
+    </div>
+  </div>
+</div>
+<div id="faq-general" class="bg-secondary-soft">
+  <div class="container py-4 py-md-5">
+    <div class="row">
+      <div class="col-12">
+        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4">General</h2>
+        <div class="card faq-card mb-3"><div class="card-body">
+          <h3 class="h5">What do you do?</h3>
+          <p>At the request of the <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/developer/core/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PostgreSQL Core Team</a>, the primary task of
+            PGCA is to manage and maintain assets (domain names and trademarks) for the PostgreSQL Project.</p>
+        </div></div>
+        <div class="card faq-card mb-3"><div class="card-body">
+          <h3 class="h5">How is the PGCA non-profit funded?</h3>
+          <p>PGCA&rsquo;s funding comes entirely from donations.</p>
+        </div></div>
+        <div class="card faq-card mb-3"><div class="card-body">
+          <h3 class="h5">Why doesn't the project manage its assets directly?</h3>
+          <p>Neither the PostgreSQL Global Development Group nor the PostgreSQL Core Team are legal entities, and thus they
+            cannot own assets, except as individuals.</p>
+        </div></div>
+        <div class="card faq-card mb-3"><div class="card-body">
+          <h3 class="h5">Where is the PGCA website’s source code?</h3>
+          <p>The full source code for this website is available in <a href="https://git.postgresql.org/gitweb?p=pgcac-website.git;a=summary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">our Git repository</a> under the PostgreSQL licence.</p>
+        </div></div>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </div>
+</div>
+<div id="faq-trademarks" class="bg-primary-soft">
+  <div class="container py-4 py-md-5">
+    <div class="row">
+      <div class="col-12">
+        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4">Trademarks</h2>
+        <div class="card faq-card mb-3"><div class="card-body">
+          <h3 class="h5">How can I use one of the PostgreSQL trademarks?</h3>
+          <p>Many uses of our marks fall under "fair use" which does not require any permission. The <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/about/policies/trademarks/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PostgreSQL Trademark Policy</a> describes these uses and general requirements. We worked very hard with our legal counsel to make the policy as flexible and permissive as possible. For uses that fall outside of the policy, a general use or tradename licence may be granted by PGCA on application.</p>
+        </div></div>
 
-  <h3>How much do you charge for trademark licences?</h3>
-  <p>There is no charge for a trademark licence. In rare cases where a non-standard agreement may be required which
-    involves significant work from counsel, we may ask for a contribution towards the cost.</p>
+        <div class="card faq-card mb-3"><div class="card-body">
+          <h3 class="h5">What are the criteria for receiving a general use or tradename licence from PGCA?</h3>
+          <p>The PGCA board evaluates several criteria for issuing a licence that falls outside of fair use, such as
+            modifications to the marks, the use of the marks within their context, would the marks create confusion with the
+            community marks, and if the usage of marks could risk bringing the project into disrepute, to name a few.</p>
+        </div></div>
 
-  <h3>Why do some other organisations have related trademarks?</h3>
-  <p>These generally fall into one of a number of categories:</p>
-  <ul>
-    <li>They are unauthorised, and may be (if appropriate) or are being disputed.</li>
